.TH DNS-QUERY 1 "2026-10-13" "SASD Freeware" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dns-query \- direct dns protocol query
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dns-query
[options] [--help | --version]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read-only direct DNS query via optional dig. Distinct from libc system resolver. A NOERROR response with an answer record is required for status 0. DNS traffic is typically unencrypted; DNSSEC validation is not performed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --name DNSNAME
DNS query name, mandatory.
.TP
.B --type TYPE
A, AAAA, MX, TXT, NS, PTR, CNAME, SOA, SRV, CAA; default A.
.TP
.B --server IP
Explicit numeric DNS server address, optional.
.TP
.B --timeout 1..10
Native query deadline in seconds; overall safety timeout is longer.
.TP
.B --help
Display help and exit.
.TP
.B --version
Display version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success/clean; 1 unsuccessful/finding; 2 invalid arguments; 3 missing prerequisites or unexpected errors.
.SH SECURITY
Only read-only checks. Query tools can send network traffic; configure only authorized targets.
